    { version = "6.3.2", text = "|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action bars: buttons without a keybind no longer show Blizzard's range dot while |cffffffffStatus Colouring|r is on; the button turns red out of range instead. With Status Colouring off, the dot is back. Thanks for the report!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Action bars: the range dot no longer shows as a \"?\" box with some keybind fonts. Thanks for the report!\n• Settings and Edit Mode: long dropdowns, such as fonts from a font pack, scroll after 20 entries instead of running off the screen. Thanks for the report!\n• Bags: |cffffffffUncollected Appearances|r only marks weapons and armour that can change your look." },
    { version = "6.3.1", text = "|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Blizzard's own text keeps its sizes again. FlareUI's settings window was changing the size of the game's fonts as soon as it loaded: buff timers, window titles, quest text and more. The new font options weren't the cause; they stay off unless you pick them. Thanks for the report!" },
    { version = "6.3", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffOne font for everything|r: a |cffffffffGlobal Font|r on the Settings page, and every font can follow it.\n• |cffffffffA font for every frame|r: unit frames, buffs, the tracker, resource bars and the minimap set their fonts in Edit Mode, frame by frame.\n• |cffffffffSmoother play|r: a pass over everything that could cause short lag spikes, above all with gathering and quest addons.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Settings › |cffffffffGlobal Font|r (Friz Quadrata TT): one font for all of FlareUI's text, set in one place.\n      - Every font dropdown now starts with |cffffffffGlobal|r, and every font that used Friz Quadrata follows it. Chat text and action bar text keep Arial Narrow.\n      - |cffffffffUse Global Font Everywhere|r sets every FlareUI font to Global. Sizes, outlines and shadows stay.\n      - |cffffffffReset All Fonts|r puts every font back to its default.\n      - |cffffffffGame Text|r (off): Blizzard's own text takes the Global Font too: menus, windows, quest text, nameplates and more.\n      - |cffffffffNameplate Font|r (Default): the names on Blizzard's nameplates.\n      - |cffffffffCombat Text Font|r (Default): the damage and healing numbers over what you hit. It changes the next time you log in.\n• Edit Mode: a |cffffffffFonts|r section, always the last one, for each frame. Pick a text, then its |cffffffffFont|r, |cffffffffOutline|r, |cffffffffShadow|r and |cffffffffSize|r.\n      - |cffffffffUnit frames|r: each frame its own fonts for |cffffffffNames|r, |cffffffffHealth Text|r, |cffffffffLevel|r, |cffffffffPower Text|r, |cffffffffCast Name|r, |cffffffffCast Countdown|r, |cffffffffAura Timers|r and |cffffffffAura Stacks|r. Party, raid and boss frames too. Each frame style keeps its own.\n      - |cffffffffPlayer Cast Bar|r: its own |cffffffffCast Name|r and |cffffffffCast Countdown|r.\n      - |cffffffffBuffs|r and |cffffffffDebuffs|r: each their own |cffffffffAura Timers|r and |cffffffffAura Stacks|r.\n      - |cffffffffBuff Reminders|r: |cffffffffCounts|r and |cffffffffTime Left|r.\n      - |cffffffffQuest Tracker|r, every |cffffffffresource bar|r and the |cffffffffminimap|r (zone name, clock and info text).\n      - |cffffffffApply to All|r gives the same fonts to every frame of the kind; |cffffffffReset Fonts|r puts the frame's back.\n• More fonts in the Fonts tabs:\n      - Action Bars › |cffffffffXP Bar|r: the bar's numbers. It used the Keybinds font before.\n      - Radial Menu: a new |cffffffffFonts|r tab with |cffffffffButton Names|r and |cffffffffCounts|r.\n      - Bags & Looting › |cffffffffGold|r: the money at the bottom of your bags.\n• Bags & Looting › Bags: |cffffffffItem Level|r (off) on weapons and armour, in their quality's colour, in your bags and on the character sheet. Thanks for the request!\n• Bags & Looting › Bags: |cffffffffUncollected Appearances|r (off): an eye on gear whose look you can still learn. Thanks for the request!\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffShow Item Level|r (off) on weapons and armour. Thanks for the request!\n• Meters › Threat: |cffffffffSeparate Window|r (off): threat in its own window, moved and sized in Edit Mode. Thanks for the request!\n• Action Bars › Bars Appearance:\n      - |cffffffffBorderless Micro Menu|r (off) and |cffffffffBorderless Bag Bar|r (off).\n      - |cffffffffCollapsible Bag Bar|r (off): an arrow beside the backpack folds the other bags away. Needs Borderless Bag Bar. Thanks for the request!\n• Unit frames › Health Text, Forever Style: |cffffffffPercent <  > Value|r: the percent at the bar's left end, the full value at its right. Thanks for the request!\n• Health Text: |cffffffffValue | Health Lost|r, such as \"1234 | -216\".\n• Radial Menu › Options: |cffffffffSub-Radials|r (Reset on Close): a sub-radial opens on its first button, or on the one you used last with |cffffffffRemember|r.\n• Minimap › Style: three cards, |cffffffffSquare (Clean)|r, |cffffffffSquare (Header)|r and |cffffffffRound|r.\n• Minimap: |cffffffffLatency|r (off), under Framerate: your home and world latency at the bottom right.\n• |cffffffffFrançais|r: French is in the language list on its own now, with every new text translated.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Edit Mode now holds the fonts of Unit Frames, Buffs & Debuffs, Minimap, Resource Bars and Quest Tracker, and their pages lost their Fonts tab. A |cffffffffFonts|r row on each page opens Edit Mode. Your fonts carry over.\n• Fonts tabs: each font starts closed, and fonts are grouped in titled sections, such as |cffffffffAction Bars|r and |cffffffffXP Bar|r.\n• Bar text choices: |cffffffffValue | Percent|r is now |cffffffffPercent | Value|r, and |cffffffffCurrent (Max)|r is now |cffffffffValue [Max]|r. |cffffffffCurrent (Max) | Percent|r is gone; it becomes Value [Max].\n• Settings › UI Scale: the |cffffffffBlizzard's|r choice is now called |cffffffffOff|r, and says that any other choice replaces Blizzard's UI Scale each time you log in. Thanks for the report!\n• Buff Reminders:\n      - Rogue poisons and other weapon buffs are recognised by kind, so Forever's reworked poisons count. Low charges start at 5. Thanks for the report!\n      - Forever's hunter aspects, Trueshot Aura, Fel Armor, elixirs, food and oils are recognised more reliably.\n      - Paladin auras and hunter aspects count only when they're yours.\n• Minimap: the Fading section opens and closes like the others.\n• Loot Rolls and Toasts: their Scale shows plain numbers.\n• Bags: clicking the keyring or reagent bag icon opens and closes the combined backpack while that bag is part of it. Thanks to parchinskiy!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Short lag spikes: FlareUI no longer handles the map pins of gathering and quest addons, and a long list of other places do less work. Thanks for the report!\n• Buffs & Debuffs: no more slowdown after using Edit Mode in a fight or an instance.\n• Fishing: |cffffffffDouble-Click to Fish|r works with Blizzard's Cast on Key Down. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: the square minimap is put back properly after ForeverFarmHUD or FarmHud; FlareUI explains the farming HUDs once. Thanks for the report!\n• Bags: the keyring and reagent sections show the new-item glow like the rest, and lose it when you close your bags. Thanks to parchinskiy!\n• Bags: a hidden reagent window no longer blocks clicks on the backpack with Move Any Window on. Thanks to parchinskiy!\n• Russian: buttons and other text show their letters with FlareUI in Russian on a game client in another language." },
    { version = "6.2", text = "|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffA settings window that looks like Blizzard's|r: Friz Quadrata text, WoW's yellow titles, and Blizzard's own checkboxes, dropdowns, sliders, buttons and scroll bars.\n• |cffffffffMinimap › Header|r: pick a headerless square minimap in a heavy bronze frame, or the bordered one with its title bar.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Minimap › Style: |cffffffffHeader|r (Headerless), for the square minimap.\n      - |cffffffffHeaderless|r: the map framed in the heavy bronze border of the settings window, its buttons and zone name on the map.\n      - |cffffffffBordered|r: the frame's bronze title bar over the map, the buttons and zone name in it, as before 6.1.1.\n      - Both are the same size, so switching doesn't move your minimap.\n• Minimap: a |cffffffffFlareUI button|r when you untick FlareUI in |cffffffffAddons in the Drawer|r. Left-click opens the settings, right-click puts FlareUI back in the drawer, drag it along the edge to move it. It never shows while the drawer is off.\n• Tooltips › Look: |cffffffffFrame Opacity|r (100%), under Scale. Thanks for the request!\n• Loot Feed: |cffffffffAlignment|r (Left). Right puts the icons on the right, with the text before them. Thanks for the request!\n• Buff Reminders, warlocks with Demonic Sacrifice and Demonic Pact: a |cffffffffDemonic Sacrifice|r reminder while you have none of its buffs, and your pet and Soul Link are still asked for. Thanks for the report!\n• What's New: |cffffffffDon't Show on Login|r (off), at the bottom of the page. These notes then stay here instead of opening after an update. Thanks for the report!\n• Settings, in Gamepad mode: options the Gamepad UI doesn't let FlareUI run are greyed, with a red note saying so. Thanks for the report!\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Settings window: a new, more Blizzard-like look.\n      - All text in Friz Quadrata, the game's own font, in white, with titles in WoW's yellow.\n      - Blizzard's own checkboxes, choice arrows, dropdowns, sliders and scroll bars.\n      - Buttons and tabs in Blizzard's grey with a bronze rim.\n      - The plain stone background, with darker boxes so the options read more easily.\n      - The module list on the left has no checkboxes; turn a module on or off beside its page title.\n• Buff Reminders › Your Own: |cffffffffCustom Reminders|r and |cffffffffHidden Reminders|r are now lists. Untick one to remove it or bring it back; |cffffffffNone|r does them all. Thanks for the request!\n• Bags & Looting: FlareUI leaves your bags alone while a bag addon runs (Bagnon, Baganator, AdiBags, ArkInventory, BetterBags, BagSmith and more), so its sorting and cleanup work as they should. Looting features keep working. Thanks for the report!\n• Action bars: druids' Prowl turns Action Bar 1 to the prowl page again, as Stealth does for rogues. |cffffffffKeep Page 1 in Stealth|r still keeps your Cat Form page.\n• Minimap › Addons in the Drawer: one line per addon, under its real name.\n• Buff Reminders: druids no longer get an Omen of Clarity reminder. It's a random proc on Forever, nothing to keep up.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: the game no longer hangs when you turn GatherLite's HUD or FarmHud on or off. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: Social Diary's button works in the addon drawer again. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap, square style: the border's shadow and corners are no longer cut off by the map.\n• Chat: TradeSkillMaster's settings no longer show an error on their General page. Thanks for the report!\n• Tooltips: Russian clients show a player's class again. Thanks for the report!\n• Fast Auto-Loot no longer stops working until a reload. Thanks for the report!\n• Cast bars: your own casts and profession casts no longer turn grey on the target or focus bar. Casts you can't interrupt still do.\n• Buff Reminders: the Passive Pet reminder no longer flashes as you dismount. Thanks for the report!" },
    { version = "6.1.1", text = "|cffffd100New|r\n• Minimap: |cffffffffAddons in the Drawer|r (all), under |cffffffffAddon Button Drawer|r: tick the addons whose buttons go in the drawer. The others are left alone on the minimap, where their addon puts them. Changes take effect after a reload.\n      - It replaces Shift+Right-Click on drawer icons, which clashed with addons' own right-click menus. Buttons you kept on the minimap that way stay out of the drawer.\n• Settings › Sync Blizz UI: |cffffffffHide Pop-up Alerts|r (off): syncs still happen, with no pop-up asking to reload, on every character. The pop-up's new |cffffffffHide These Alerts|r button turns it on.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Minimap, square style: addon buttons left out of the drawer sit on the border, packed along the bottom from beside the sundial. Drag one along the border and it stays where you drop it, through every reload. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap, square style: the bronze border is drawn under the map, so no addon button can end up beneath it.\n• Unit frames › player frame › Visibility: |cffffffffMissing Health|r and |cffffffffMissing Mana|r can no longer be ticked together; ticking one unticks the other. The game hides both from addons, so the two can't be combined. If you had both, Missing Mana stays. Thanks for the report!\n• Action bars: |cffffffffActive Highlight|r follows the button's own frame, round corners and all, instead of a square. Thanks for the report!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: the |cffffffffMiddle-Click Menu|r opens again. Other clicks ping the map as usual. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: addon buttons no longer move around on every reload, and RareScanner's button shows again when left out of the drawer. Thanks for the report!\n• Resource bars: Blizzard's own swing timer no longer appears in busy fights when FlareUI's swing bars are on. Thanks for the report!\n• Unit frames: the player frame now fades as it should with Missing Health and Missing Mana both set (see Changed). Thanks for the report!" },
